# Worktrees: a second checkout of this repository, made by whichever tool is
# running parallel work. Never part of a commit -- a worktree is a checkout, not
# content, and `git add -A` in the main checkout would otherwise stage a whole
# second tree of the files that are already tracked.
#
# The canonical location is `.worktree/` at the repository root (owner decision
# 2026-09-17). The remaining patterns are the older spellings, kept so a checkout
# left under one of them can never be staged. Git's own registration lives under
# `.git/`, which is never committed in the first place; this is about the working
# copy.
/.worktree/
worktrees/
.worktrees/
*.worktree/

